      "title": "Fairfax Financial Holdings Limited Reportedly Leads Race to Acquire Majority Stake in IDBI Bank from Govt, LIC",
      "body": "The government's long-running plan to exit IDBI Bank Limited (NSEI:IDBI) has reached a crucial stage, with Toronto-based Fairfax Financial Holdings Limited (TSX:FFH) now seen as the strongest contender for a majority takeover, according to a report by The Economic Times. The company is ahead of rival bidder Kotak Mahindra Bank Limited (BSE:500247) as the deadline for submitting financial offers approaches. The union government and Life Insurance Corporation of India (NSEI:LICI) (LIC) together plan to sell 60.72% stake, valued at nearly $7,000 million at current market prices. Fairfax, Kotak shortlisted from earlier round. Only two serious bidders -- Fairfax Financial and Kotak Mahindra Bank -- remain in the race. Both were shortlisted after expressing interest when the privatisation proces",
